{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 38, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a 2010 american biographical drama film directed by david finch errol, written by grant heslov, alexandre dlaszlo, and jared leto, and produced by finch errol and scott ranger. the film is based on the 2009 book the facebook effect by ben messinguh and diego argellos, which chronicles the founding and initial rise of facebook.\n\nthe movie revolves around the life of mark zuckerberg, a young college student who created the popular social networking site facebook from his dorm room while attending harvard university. the film explores the events that led to the creation of facebook, including zuckerberg's relationships with his roommates and fellow students eduardo saverin, and andre andrew mcgee.\n\none of the standout aspects of the film is its attention to detail, with the production team meticulously recreating the setting of harvard's campus and incorporating real-life events and figures into the narrative. the film also features an impressive cast, including jesse eisenberg as zuckerberg, forrest whitaker as sean parker, and armie hamer as mark kydland.\n\nthe cinematography is also noteworthy, capturing the intensity and passion of the characters as they navigate the challenges of creating a revolutionary new platform. the film's score, composed by tic tac touchee, perfectly complements the on-screen action, adding to the overall sense of tension and excitement.\n\nthe performances in the film are also excellent, with jesse eisenberg delivering a convincing portrayal of zuckerberg as a brilliant and driven young man, but also as someone struggling with the pressures and expectations of fame and success. armie hamer, in particular, gives a standout performance as mark kydland, the person who serves as the catalyst for zuckerberg's decision to drop out of college and focus on facebook full-time.\n\nthe film received widespread critical acclaim upon its release, with many praising its thought-provoking exploration of the consequences of success and the complexities of relationships. the film was also a commercial success, grossing over $224 million at the box office.\n\nif there is one criticism to be made of the film, it is that the supporting characters are somewhat one-dimensional, with the exception of eduardo saverin, played by andrew garfield. however, this is a minor quibble in what otherwise is a compelling and engaging film that sheds light on a pivotal moment in modern history.\n\noverall, the social network is a gripping and thought-provoking film that explores the complexities of success, friendship, and the consequences of creating something new and innovative. with its impressive cast, meticulous production values, and well-crafted narrative, the film is a must-see for anyone interested in the story behind facebook and its impact on modern society.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.20552276074886322}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.00030310326837934554}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.04680052399635315}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0009606037638150156}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.5348334312438965}, {"token": "201", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "0", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " american", "logprob": -0.2830283045768738}, {"token": " bi", "logprob": -0.014159570448100567}, {"token": "ographical", "logprob": -2.2053474822314456e-05}, {"token": " drama", "logprob": -0.00047052756417542696}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.00013386306818574667}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.09783122688531876}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -0.0008936702506616712}, {"token": " david", "logprob": -0.04422512650489807}, {"token": " fin", "logprob": -1.680836794548668e-05}, {"token": "ch", "logprob": -1.791347861289978}, {"token": " er", "logprob": -0.41596129536628723}, {"token